<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- App-host Activity theme for the C++ MAUI gallery on Android.

     WHY THIS EXISTS (parity):
     The Activity previously declared NO android:theme. With targetSdkVersion 34 that makes the framework
     apply Theme.DeviceDefault (Material You / Material3) on API-34 devices, whose ?android:colorBackground
     resolves to the Material3 *tonal surface* — a very slightly purple-tinted white (measured #F1F0F7 on
     the maui-test emulator). Real .NET MAUI (MauiAppCompatActivity + Maui.MainTheme, whose base parent is
     Theme.MaterialComponents.DayNight) renders these native-default ContentPages on a PURE WHITE window
     background (#FFFFFF) in light mode. That mismatch is what the parity review flagged as "port page
     background is light lavender-gray vs MAUI's white" (content_view, menu_bar, and every sparse page).

     TWO FIXES PINNED HERE:

     (1) NO ACTION BAR (2026-07-01). We previously parented on DeviceDefault.Light.DarkActionBar and KEPT
     the action bar — it painted a top app-title bar showing android:label ("MAUI C++ Gallery"). Real
     .NET MAUI's Android gallery renders these ContentPages with NO such top bar (its shell/toolbar is
     empty on these native-default pages), so the port's title bar was a parity DIFF. Per the parity
     policy (MAUI's render is the ground truth), we now parent on the NoActionBar framework theme, so the
     content starts directly below the status bar — exactly where a native-default MAUI ContentPage's
     content starts. app_host.cpp's content_chrome_height_px NO LONGER reserves action-bar height; it
     subtracts only the status bar (top) + navigation bar (bottom), so the page layout still positions
     correctly under this theme.

     (2) WHITE BACKGROUND. Pin the window / colorBackground to pure white so it matches MAUI's rendered
     background exactly, instead of inheriting the DeviceDefault/Material3 tonal surface (#F1F0F7
     lavender). We parent on the framework DeviceDefault.Light.NoActionBar (no Material Components AAR on
     the app-host classpath — the app-host links android.jar only, no gradle). -->
<resources>
    <style name="MauiAppHost.Theme" parent="@android:style/Theme.DeviceDefault.Light.NoActionBar">
        <!-- Match MAUI's white light-mode page background (Theme.MaterialComponents.DayNight resolves to
             white), instead of the DeviceDefault/Material3 tonal surface (#F1F0F7 lavender). Both the
             window drawable and the colorBackground attribute are pinned so surfaces that read either one
             land on pure white. -->
        <item name="android:windowBackground">@android:color/white</item>
        <item name="android:colorBackground">@android:color/white</item>
    </style>
</resources>
